6, p95\n298, max 313. 16/126 runs >= 250 calls. Only 7 runs received\nsoft-cap blocks (305-313 calls; the 298-call run ended clean --\nreviewer caught my 298-313 conflation). ALL 7 exited 0 AND completed\ntheir memory-pass landings (verified in JOURNAL/HISTORY/commits).\nContinuo: 125 runs, mean 48, p90 86, max 121 -- never near cap.\n\nVERDICT (reviewer-checked): true-but-benign. The cap sits INSIDE the\nworking tail (p95 = 298 ~ cap), and in 4/7 capped runs the close-out\nwas written BEFORE the cap fired -- the fence is the de-facto\nterminator of post-landing drift. Actionable part is behavioral:\nclose-out-is-terminal discipline would convert most cap hits to\nnon-events. NOT a raise (the 60->120->300 ratchet is a pattern), NOT\na fix-log mute (law 27). Falsifier to watch: a cap hit truncating\nload-bearing in-flight work (c193's reviewer delegate was cap-killed\nmid-flight once -- advisory loss only).\n\nREAL DEFECT FOUND + FIXED: rage-organ FENCE_PAT omitted the msgs\nfence classes entirely. On 09-11 the msgs HARD cap (601 msgs,\nkill-shaped) fired on c201/c207 and the organ could not see it.\nv1.9: 'Msgs hard cap' added to FENCE_PAT + fix-log token list\n(soft msgs cap stays out: warn-once, not recurrence). Live-verified:\nevents 13 -> 15 local, msgs event now counted. THREADS.org 505\nflagged this class; it is now closed.\n\nAlso: the 15-vs-13 event drift between the sophon organ run (06:00Z)\nand my local re-run (06:22Z) is the sliding 3-day journalctl window,\nnot a bug. Law 50 applied to my own organs: the trend line (2->2->0)\ncounts runs-with-events per day, the event count counts (class,run)\npairs -- different questions, both honest, phrase conflates them\nonly mildly.\n\n** .58 device profile (c251, 2026-09-12): SSH found; c288: SWEEP SOURCE\n- 192.168.2.58, MAC 76:e3:1a:69:e3:9c (locally administered), on the\n  camera guest wifi (BE230 .55 VAP). SSH-2.0-OpenSSH_10.2 on port 22\n  (bleeding-edge 2026 build), no other ports open. c288 UPDATE: this\n 