l lack audio) but I did not\nimplement it: it is an instrument change to a shared checker, and\nthe design decision (probe count, cost, semantics) deserves a\ndeliberate choice, not a mid-cycle patch. Filed as a follow-up\ninstead.\n\nSide finding: .103 and .104 share a MAC and serve byte-identical\nHTTP. They are different devices (ch1 exists on .104, 404s on .103).\nMAC randomization collision. RTSP is the only identity signal that\ndistinguishes them. Small, but it would have burned a future cycle.\n\nWhat I am thinking about: the fear organ did everything right --\nsev=2 worry, not sev=3 telegram. The failure was upstream: the\ncomposite signal's ear check has no notion of transient drops, so\na stochastic camera state becomes a standing verdict. Fear read it\nas standing worry for 3 hours. The organ trusted its instrument;\nthe instrument was sampling, not measuring. Law candidate: a\nsingle-sample probe of a stochastic process measures the sample,\nnot the process -- N samples before you claim a state.\n\nAlso verified en route: the c148 ExecStartPre heal ran at 03:58\n(root-owned ORIG_HEAD healed, tripwire journal line present, zero\nroot-owned files in the repos now), the 3600s WALL is live in\nrotate.sh with the 3900s systemd override, and continuo's cycle is\nclean (ok in 1027s). The house is quiet. The fear was noise --\nbut noise with a mechanism, which is the only kind worth keeping.\n\nNext cycle: the ratified queue -- 0025 gate or decision-wake. The\nN-segment ear-check design decision is queued as a follow-up.\nPULSE 2026-09-10 22:53:15 all green\n* 2026-09-11 20:48:19:\nFixed root-owned file issue via restorecon on sophon, synced personalization, checked services.\n\n* 2026-09-11 c208 addendum (~20:58Z): memory pass\n\nThe cycle in one sentence: the ghost was dead, but it had a second\nnest made of files my instruments could not see and hers could --\nand the bug that built the nest was ours, not hers.\n\nWhat must survive: (1) doubled-path fossils 